# The reference daemon's (examples/reference-bridge) PICS declarations that
# cannot be read off the device. See docs/certifiability.md and
# docs/adr/0011-certifiability-is-a-goal.md.
#
# The PICS a case runs with is composed, in this order:
#   1. CHIP's ci-pics-values — for the codes this file and the device do not
#      decide (client-side .C codes the DUT never acts on, PIXIT-like
#      switches, PICS_* runner controls);
#   2. this file;
#   3. the device-generated slice of the endpoint under test
#      (testdata/pics/ep<N>.txt, written by testdata/gen_pics.py from a
#      wildcard read with CHIP's own derivation helpers). Every server-side
#      cluster, attribute, command, feature and event code of every spec
#      cluster is in it, 0 or 1, together with the derivable MCORE codes.
#
# This file may not set a code the generated slices carry — the suite fails
# if it does, so a declaration here can never contradict the device. A line
# here is a statement about the daemon a reader can check in the code named
# next to it. TC-IDM-10.4 (TC_pics_checker) holds slices + this file against
# the device on every endpoint.

# --- Runner controls ---------------------------------------------------------
# PICS_SDK_CI_ONLY stays 1 for the family runs: it gates steps that need the
# CHIP sample apps' test hooks, which the daemon does not have. The TC-IDM-10.4
# runs set it to 0, as a certification PICS must. The YAML SystemCommands
# steps it gates (Reboot, FactoryReset) are answered by the suite's
# accessory server (accessory_test.go). PICS_SKIP_SAMPLE_APP stays 0, the
# value of CHIP's ci-pics-values that matter.js runs with: the steps it gates
# are operator prompts standing in for the hooks that accessory server
# provides (TC-GRPKEY-2.2 step 21 asks an operator to fill GroupKeyMap,
# TC-OO-2.4 to confirm a reboot), which an unattended run cannot answer.
PICS_USER_PROMPT=0
PICS_SKIP_SAMPLE_APP=0

# --- Transport and roles (examples/reference-bridge/main.go, transport/udp) --
# IPv6 UDP over Ethernet/IP only; no Bluetooth, Thread or Wi-Fi commissioning
# (scope decision, CLAUDE.md), no TCP transport (mdns/service.go advertises T=0).
MCORE.COM.ETH=1
MCORE.COM.WIFI=0
MCORE.COM.THR=0
MCORE.COM.BLE=0
MCORE.COM.WIRELESS=0
MCORE.SC.S.TCP=0
MCORE.ROLE.COMMISSIONER=0
MCORE.ROLE.CONTROLLER=0
MCORE.IDM.C=0
MCORE.BRIDGECLIENT=0
MCORE.DEVLIST.UseDevices=0
MCORE.DEVLIST.UseDeviceState=0
MCORE.DEVLIST.UseDeviceName=0
MCORE.DEVLIST.UseBatInfo=0

# --- Bridge (bridge/, examples/reference-bridge/fleet*.go) -------------------
# Bridged endpoints carry BridgedDeviceBasicInformation with a writable
# NodeLabel; the smoke alarm bridges a PowerSource with battery state.
MCORE.BRIDGE.AllowDeviceRename=1
MCORE.BRIDGE.BatInfo=1
MCORE.BRIDGE.OtherControl=0

# --- Onboarding (examples/reference-bridge/main.go printOnboarding) ---------
# The daemon prints a QR code and an 11-digit manual code; it has no NFC tag,
# no UI, no physical tamper or lock, and is commissionable on the network
# right after start (standard flow).
MCORE.DD.QR=1
MCORE.DD.MANUAL_PC=1
MCORE.DD.11_MANUAL_PC=1
MCORE.DD.21_MANUAL_PC=0
MCORE.DD.NFC=0
MCORE.DD.PASSCODE=1
MCORE.DD.UI=0
MCORE.DD.CHIP_DEV=1
MCORE.DD.DEV_LOCK=0
MCORE.DD.DEV_BARRIER=0
MCORE.DD.PHYSICAL_TAMPERING=0
MCORE.DD.STANDARD_COMM_FLOW=1
MCORE.DD.USER_INTENT_COMM_FLOW=0
MCORE.DD.CUSTOM_COMM_FLOW=0
MCORE.DD.DISCOVERY_BLE=0
MCORE.DD.DISCOVERY_PAF=0
MCORE.DD.EXTENDED_DISCOVERY=0
MCORE.DD.CONCATENATED_QR_CODE=0
# Controller-side DD codes: the DUT is not a commissioner.
MCORE.DD.CONTROLLER=0
MCORE.DD.COMM_DISCOVERY=0
MCORE.DD.SCAN_NFC=0
MCORE.DD.SCAN_QR_CODE=0
MCORE.DD.MANUAL_PC_COMMISSIONING=0
MCORE.DD.QR_COMMISSIONING=0
MCORE.DD.CTRL_CONCATENATED_QR_CODE_1=0
MCORE.DD.CTRL_CONCATENATED_QR_CODE_1_INORDER=0
MCORE.DD.CTRL_CONCATENATED_QR_CODE_2=0

# --- DNS-SD TXT keys and subtypes (mdns/service.go) --------------------------
# Commissionable: D, CM, DT, VP, DN (the node label), SII/SAI/SAT, PH, RI
# (examples/reference-bridge/main.go wires a rotating id); no PI. Subtypes
# _L, _S, _CM, _T, _V.
MCORE.DD.TXT_KEY_VP=1
MCORE.DD.TXT_KEY_DT=1
MCORE.DD.TXT_KEY_DN=1
MCORE.DD.TXT_KEY_RI=1
MCORE.DD.TXT_KEY_PH=1
MCORE.DD.TXT_KEY_PI=0
MCORE.DD.COMMISSIONING_SUBTYPE_V=1
MCORE.DD.COMMISSIONING_SUBTYPE_T=1
MCORE.SC.VP_KEY=1
MCORE.SC.DT_KEY=1
MCORE.SC.DN_KEY=1
MCORE.SC.RI_KEY=1
MCORE.SC.PH_KEY=1
MCORE.SC.PI_KEY=0
MCORE.SC.T_KEY=1
MCORE.SC.SII_COMM_DISCOVERY_KEY=1
MCORE.SC.SAI_COMM_DISCOVERY_KEY=1
MCORE.SC.SII_OP_DISCOVERY_KEY=1
MCORE.SC.SAI_OP_DISCOVERY_KEY=1
MCORE.SC.VENDOR_SUBTYPE=1
MCORE.SC.DEVTYPE_SUBTYPE=1
MCORE.SC.EXTENDED_DISCOVERY=0
MCORE.SC.SED=0
MCORE.SC.ADV=1
MCORE.SC.LWIP=0

# --- OTA, BDX, file system ---------------------------------------------------
# The reference daemon mounts no OTA Software Update Requestor or Provider and
# no Diagnostic Logs, so it speaks no BDX.
MCORE.OTA.HTTPS=0
MCORE.OTA.RequestorConsent=0
MCORE.OTA.Resume=0
MCORE.OTA.VendorSpecific=0
MCORE.OTA.Retry=0
MCORE.BDX.Driver=0
MCORE.BDX.BlockQueryWithSkip=0
MCORE.FS=0
MCORE.UI.FACTORYRESET=0
MCORE.DT_SW_COMP=0

# --- Device attestation (examples/reference-bridge/wiring.go) ---------------
# Test DAC chain and a test Certification Declaration without dac_origin
# fields or firmware information.
MCORE.DA.CERTDECL_ORIGIN_VENDORID=0
MCORE.DA.CERTDECL_ORIGIN_PRODUCTID=0
MCORE.DA.CERTDECL_AUTH_PAA=0
MCORE.DA.ATTESTELEMENT_FW_INFO=0
MCORE.DA.ATTEST_WARNING=0

# --- Interaction model, server side ------------------------------------------
# Subscriptions are persisted and re-established after a restart
# (bridge/subscription_reestablish.go).
MCORE.IDM.S.PersistentSubscription=1

# --- Optional events the daemon emits ----------------------------------------
# The slices carry the mandatory events; these are the optional ones the
# servers emit (EventList is not served, so they cannot be read off the
# device). Each applies on the endpoints whose slice has the cluster.
# BasicInformation.ShutDown / Leave: examples/reference-bridge/main.go fires
# them on shutdown and when a fabric is removed.
BINFO.S.E01=1
BINFO.S.E02=1
# OperationalState.OperationCompletion: cluster/opstate
# Server.EmitOperationCompletion, which the laundry washer of
# examples/reference-bridge/fleet_appliances.go fires when its cycle ends;
# the device type mandates it (TC-OPSTATE-2.5). The robot vacuum emits none.
OPSTATE.S.E01=1
# RvcOperationalState.OperationCompletion: the robot vacuum emits it when a
# cleaning run ends (RvcRunMode Cleaning -> Idle,
# examples/reference-bridge/fleet_appliances.go); the device type mandates it.
# CHIP's slice derivation (gen_pics.py, matter/testing/pics.py) decides event
# codes from cluster conformance only — EventList is not read back — so an
# event a device type mandates is declared here, as OperationCompletion is
# above.
RVCOPSTATE.S.E01=1
# PumpConfigurationAndControl DryRunning (0x05) and PumpBlocked (0x09): the
# pump declares both (examples/reference-bridge/fleet_climate.go Events) and
# raises them through the app pipe (PumpEvent, control.go).
PCC.S.E05=1
PCC.S.E09=1
# SmokeCoAlarm AlarmMuted, MuteEnded, InterconnectSmokeAlarm and
# InterconnectCoAlarm: the alarm serves DeviceMuted and both interconnect
# attributes (fleet_safety.go), so cluster/alarm lists and emits the events
# (smokecoalarm_server.go MatterEvents, Refresh).
SMOKECO.S.E06=1
SMOKECO.S.E07=1
SMOKECO.S.E08=1
SMOKECO.S.E09=1
# The robot vacuum takes the rvc-app's manual controls through the app pipe
# (examples/reference-bridge/control.go: Reset, ChargerFound, Charged,
# Docked, ErrorEvent), which TC-RVCOPSTATE-2.4 drives.
RVCOPSTATE.S.M.CAN_MANUALLY_CONTROLLED=1

# --- Window covering modes -------------------------------------------------
# The blind has no calibration procedure (cluster/cover; matter.js
# WindowCoveringServer supportsCalibration defaults to false) and the module
# does not implement maintenance mode (open finding, by TC id in
# notes/parity/matter_behaviour_findings.md).
WNCV.S.M.Calibration=0
WNCV.S.M.Maintenance=0

# --- Client roles -------------------------------------------------------------
# The daemon is a server for every cluster it mounts and a client of none: it
# never sends OnOff, ColorControl, WindowCovering, SoftwareDiagnostics or
# EthernetNetworkDiagnostics commands. CHIP's ci-pics-values declares those
# clients for its sample apps (DGSW.C=1 at :49, DGETH.C=1 at :1144 at the
# harness pin), which would run the DUT-as-client cases
# (Test_TC_*_Simulated; TC-DGSW-3.2 and TC-DGETH-3.2 wait for the DUT to send
# ResetWatermarks / ResetCounts, PICS DGSW.C / DGETH.C) against a DUT that
# issues no command.
OO.C=0
CC.C=0
WNCV.C=0
DGSW.C=0
DGETH.C=0

# --- Door lock writable attributes (cluster/lock) ---------------------------
# The lock serves LockState, LockType, ActuatorEnabled, OperatingMode
# (writable) and SupportedOperatingModes; the optional settings attributes
# below are not served, so none of them is writable. CHIP's ci-pics-values
# declares them writable for its sample lock.
DRLK.S.M.LanguageAttributeWritable=0
DRLK.S.M.LEDSettingsAttributeWritable=0
DRLK.S.M.AutoRelockTimeAttributeWritable=0
DRLK.S.M.SoundVolumeAttributeWritable=0
DRLK.S.M.LocalProgrammingFeaturesAttributeWritable=0
DRLK.S.M.WrongCodeEntryLimitAttributeWritable=0
DRLK.S.M.UserCodedTemporaryDisableTimeAttributeWritable=0
DRLK.S.M.RequirePINForRemoteOperationAttributeWritable=0
